- op: discuss  # 8c25
  at: '2026-07-22T01:06:17Z'  # 8c25
  by: agent  # 8c25
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8c25
  clock: 6  # 8c25
  nonce: 8c25  # 8c25
  message: "G1 investigation (read-only, PR #808 session): premise TRUE. TWO patterns. Pattern A (6 linker families — subprocess_call/db_query/mq_publisher+subscriber/http_client/resolver/ws-endpoint, ~236 nodes): the id name-slot carries a GENERIC linker-category constant while node.name carries the SPECIFIC value; ALSO the not-enumerated graphql_client (linkers/graphql.py:209) + grpc_stub/client (grpc.py:721). Pattern B (Starlette route, py.py:3060-3066): INVERTED — id name-slot has the specific method+path, node.name has a generic 'starlette:<view>'. FIX DIRECTION = ALIGN (ADR-0036 Ruling 1: id name-slot MUST equal sanitized(Symbol.name); this is the deferred T1 producer-side landing). Deferred here (T1: node.id VALUE churn for those synthetic nodes — stable_id UNAFFECTED, no scheme bump). Sanitization (:→.) belongs at the make_symbol_id chokepoint. Test to update: test_websocket.py:325-338 hardcodes name-slot ids. Starlette (Pattern B) needs a route-naming decision -> fold into WI-zugob's proposed make_route_symbol chokepoint, NOT the linker fix. Ready to implement as a focused PR (Pattern-A linkers) + coordinate Pattern B with WI-zugob."  # 8c25
- op: discuss  # 68fc
  at: '2026-07-28T04:18:08Z'  # 68fc
  by: agent  # 68fc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 68fc
  clock: 7  # 68fc
  nonce: 68fc  # 68fc
  message: "PR #44 (dev 660be7bd8a): Pattern A landed for 6 of the synthetic-node families — subprocess_call/db_query/http_client/graphql_client/resolver/mq_publisher+subscriber. Each factory now routes Symbol.name through the new sanitize_id_name_segment helper (analyze/base.py; ':'->'.', ADR-0036 Ruling 1) into the id name-slot, replacing the generic category constant. Evidence: test_synthetic_node_id_name_slot.py asserts _name_slot(sym.id)==sanitize_id_name_segment(sym.name) across all 6 factories (incl. the filed subprocess 'git config' repro shape) + a category-constant guard; full affected slice green, 100% cov. SCOPE NARROWED from the pt.34 'make_symbol_id chokepoint' plan: an always-on make_symbol_id sanitization also rewrites colon-bearing SOURCE ids (Obj-C selectors removeItemAtPath:error:) = the broader deferred WI-sikar — caught by test_objc regressions in the affected slice — so the helper is scoped to the synthetic stand-ins + a guard test (test_make_symbol_id_does_not_sanitize_globally) blocks the global change returning. RESIDUAL (stays open): (a) websocket ws-endpoint (its wrapper builds the slot from event+kind-suffix not node.name — route-vs-URL naming decision); (b) grpc stub/client/route (grpc.py local _make_symbol_id emits non-canonical 'grpc:{file}:{line}:{name}:{kind}' — a separate malformed-id bug). Both deferred to a follow-up."  # 68fc
- op: discuss  # 71bc
  at: '2026-07-29T04:53:36Z'  # 71bc
  by: agent  # 71bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 71bc
  clock: 8  # 71bc
  nonce: 71bc  # 71bc
  message: "PATTERN B PREMISE CORRECTED (PR #63, dev 7f285e1102) -- it is NOT Starlette-\nspecific, and it does NOT need a naming decision.\n\n(1) NOT STARLETTE-SPECIFIC. The 2026-07-22 note scoped Pattern B to\n\"Starlette route, py.py:3060-3066 (INVERTED -- id name-slot has the specific\nmethod+path, node.name has a generic 'starlette:<view>')\". A measured sweep of\nthe route-parity corpus found the SAME inversion in go.py, which mints route\nmarkers inline with name=handler_name against an id name-slot built from\n\"{METHOD} {path}\" (live: go:main.go:8-8:ANY /users:function, name='listUsers').\nDjango (py.py:3052) has it too (name=f\"django:{view_name}\"). So Pattern B is the\nfleet-wide route-marker shape, not one producer -- and go sits INSIDE the trio\nWI-tufil certified clean, because that gate never checked the name-slot.\n\n(2) THE NAMING DECISION ALREADY EXISTS. This item deferred Pattern B pending a\n\"route-naming decision\"; framework_patterns.materialize_route_symbols (the\nWI-tufil landing) already set the convention: name = \"{METHOD} {path}\", id\nderived from it. Adopted into the new `analyze.base.make_route_symbol`\nchokepoint. It is also FORCED, not a style pick: multi-method registrations emit\nseveral markers at one span, so a handler-derived name-slot collides their ids.\nNo owner call was needed.\n\nFIX DIRECTION for Pattern B is therefore: route the producer through\nmake_route_symbol (name = \"{METHOD} {path}\", handler into meta[\"handler_ref\"]),\nNOT \"align the id name-slot to the existing node.name\". Tracked as the producer\nsweep on WI-zugob.\n\nRESIDUAL (a) ws-endpoint -- unchanged, still open here.\nRESIDUAL (b) grpc CONFIRMED and sharpened: linkers/grpc.py:417 `_make_symbol_id`\nemits \"grpc:{file_path}:{line}:{name}:{kind}\". Two independent id_format breaks,\nnot one: 'grpc' occupies the {lang} slot (not a language), and {line} is a BARE\nLINE where the canonical grammar wants {start}-{end}. Both are INV-dulah\nviolations reachable without touching route semantics -- the cheapest remaining\nslice of this item."  # 71bc
